<AtTheTable>

Do not promote an unusual weak hand because it felt hard to make. Compare the actual best fives. Use frequency tables for understanding the deck and conditional equity for decisions against an opponent.

</AtTheTable>

<QuantCorner>

Rarity and desirability are separate properties of an outcome. A rare trading result is not automatically profitable, just as a rare final card pattern is not automatically strong. Specify the payoff or comparison rule separately from its frequency.

</QuantCorner>
